summary: Root jobs run in unconfined_service_t and keep confined programs' output
description: |
    Runs the exact systemd-run invocation the executor builds for a root
    job (internal/executor Systemd.Args) on a real systemd with SELinux
    enforcing. Without SELinuxContext=, the job's shell runs in initrc_t,
    and programs with their own domain (ip, ping, nmap) lose their stdout
    and stderr to /dev/null when they start (tt/peon#3).
test: ./test.sh
duration: 5m
require:
  - systemd
  - iproute
  - iputils
  - policycoreutils
